projective specialization, binary-field representations and timings assuming
an already available group. These do not measure candidate generation. Its
June 1997 draft citation supplies no rejection log. Inspected sections: 3.4,
4.3–4.4, 6 and reference A97.

Existing exact metadata independently confirms all 21 representatives have
a=p-3. A predicate requiring only that identity accepts both omitted and
published sets. Actual operand-dependent timing and unpublished implementations
remain unmeasured. Binary-field representations do not classify these inputs.

